<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00PG">Example <span data-tag="00PG">2.5.2.7</span>.</a> Let $B_{\bullet }\operatorname{Ch}(\operatorname{\mathbf{Z}})$ denote the classifying simplicial set of the monoidal category of chain complexes. For each nonnegative integer $n \geq 0$, we can use the analysis of Remark <a data-tag="00P8" href="/tag/00P8">2.5.1.18</a> to identify $n$-simplices of $B_{\bullet }\operatorname{Ch}(\operatorname{\mathbf{Z}})$ with differential graded categories $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ satisfying $\operatorname{Ob}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) = \{  0, 1, \cdots , n \} $ and </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(i, j)_{\ast } = \begin{cases}  \operatorname{\mathbf{Z}}[0] &amp;  \text{ if } i = j \\  0 &amp;  \text{ if } i &gt; j. \end{cases} \]
</div>
